<article class="env-situation" id="0BKC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BKC">Situation <span data-tag="0BKC">15.93.15</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. Let $I = (f_1, \ldots , f_ r) \subset A$. Let $K_ n^\bullet = K_\bullet (A, f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n)$ be the Koszul complex on $f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n$ viewed as a cochain complex in degrees $-r, -r + 1, \ldots , 0$. Using the functoriality of Lemma <a href="/tag/0624" data-tag="0624">15.29.3</a> we obtain an inverse system </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \ldots \to K_3^\bullet \to K_2^\bullet \to K_1^\bullet  \]
</div>
  <p> compatible with the inverse system $H^0(K_ n^\bullet ) = A/(f_1^ n, \ldots , f_ r^ n)$ and compatible with the maps $A \to K_ n^\bullet $. </p>
</article>